# Each app has its own documented environment file:
#   back/.env.example   -> copy to back/.env        (API: database, Redis, secrets, e-mail, S3, OAuth)
#   front/.env.example  -> copy to front/.env.local (web: API URL, public site URL, default locale)
#
# docker-compose.yml reads back/.env for the api service and overrides the
# hostnames (postgres, redis, s3) for the container network.
#
# Development infrastructure credentials used by docker-compose (DEV ONLY):
#   PostgreSQL: market / market, databases "market" and "market_test"
#   Redis:      no password
#   S3 (SeaweedFS): devaccesskey / devsecretkey (docker/seaweedfs/s3.json), http://localhost:8333,
#                   bucket "market" is created by the API on startup, anonymous read allowed
